t8n|n|An inlet of the sea, usually smaller than a gulf, but of the same general character. ; A small body of water set off from the main body; as a compartment containing water for a wheel; the portion of a canal just outside of the gates of a lock, etc. ; A recess or indentation shaped like a bay. ; A principal compartment of the walls, roof, or other part of a building, or of the whole building, as marked off by the buttresses, vaulting, mullions of a window, etc.; one of the main divisions of any structure, as the part of a bridge between two piers. ; A compartment in a barn, for depositing hay, or grain in the stalks. ; A kind of mahogany obtained from Campeachy Bay. ; A berry, particularly of the laurel. ; The laurel tree (Laurus nobilis). Hence, in the plural, an honorary garland or crown bestowed as a prize for victory or excellence, anciently made or consisting of branches of the laurel. ; A tract covered with bay trees. ; A bank or dam to keep back water.	a:3w6l,148,96;5y9i,132,4;5yws,129,4;9e6n,127,59;11xr,124,69;66x9,121,3;10l0,118,4;5yob,117,2;1uuz,116,3;xh6,110,1;yxe,110,11;1a4t,109,5;3zwi,109,1;5yq6,109,1;5j69,108,1~6oy5,86,279;47au,101,154;3uj8,50,140;3leo,65,97;3w6l,148,96;782h,78,84;8nwv,78,82;11xr,124,69;43ai,21,61;5oul,59,60;9e6n,127,59;53yv,17,53;5hu9,9,50;75ig,85,40;8nsc,75,37	v:5y9i,122,2;5j69,118,2;1uuz,110,2;5yq6,109,1;3jzw,103,2;6itx,95,8;11xr,91,7;2kcp,89,60;11lw,85,4;3gik,83,1;8lri,82,6;29l5,75,3;4r8n,72,2;3tz9,71,6;9e6n,68,1~2kcp,89,60;5byn,25,35;6wqv,64,22;2nj9,67,21;8nwv,56,18;53k9,43,17;1l16,52,15;2nm0,8,14;6ys4,32,9;6itx,95,8;11xr,91,7;3tz9,71,6;2wi1,20,6;8lri,82,6;75ig,55,5	V:agpj,82,13;89dt,81,6;92a1,74,1;4r8n,62,1;8e99,62,4;5629,52,102;8mq2,44,2;551s,44,1;593n,44,24;9sm0,40,6;7qmc,40,7;824q,31,1;1cpp,30,6;7w0r,25,17;55vc,21,3~5629,52,102;593n,44,24;7w0r,25,17;agpj,82,13;7qmc,40,7;9sm0,40,6;89dt,81,6;1cpp,30,6;8e99,62,4;13o7,10,4;55vc,21,3;8mq2,44,2;92a1,74,1;551s,44,1;391f,18,1	n:1gjq,150,100;5yq6,140,9;140g,138,7;5y9i,138,6;9e6n,1